{"qid":"Q159856","names":["Duchy of Brabant"],"title":"Duchy of Brabant","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Duchy of Brabant was a major territorial state in the medieval Low Countries, elevated from the Landgraviate of Brabant to a duchy in 1183–1190 and centered on Brussels and Leuven. At its peak under Duke John I (r. 1267–1294), Brabant dominated Flemish-Walloon trade routes and won the Battle of Worringen (1288), which attached the Duchy of Limburg and made Brabant the foremost power between the Rhine and Meuse. The duchy passed by marriage to the House of Valois-Burgundy under Philip the Good in 1430, and was incorporated into the Burgundian Netherlands, ultimately becoming part of the Habsburg inheritance.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Brabant's territorial extent is well-documented through medieval charters and cartography; boundaries within the Low Countries are clearly established.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Duchy of Brabant","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Brabant"},{"label":"Wikipedia: John I, Duke of Brabant","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_I,_Duke_of_Brabant"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Battle of Worringen","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Worringen"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Burgundian Netherlands","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgundian_Netherlands"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Landgraviate of Brabant","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Henry III, Duke of Brabant","nativeName":"Hendrik III van Brabant","roman":"","start":1248,"end":1261,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Henry IV, Duke 